<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baghel</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Baghel Rajputs, Vaghela</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Baghels or Vaghelas are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> clan regarded as a branch of the Solanki (Chaulukya) of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>. A Vaghela dynasty ruled Gujarat in the 13th century, and a Baghel line established itself in the Baghelkhand region of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, where its rulers held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandhavgarh">Bandhavgarh</a> and later the princely state of Rewa until 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baghel.jpg" alt="Baghel" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Syedzohaibullah · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Purva_Falls_formed_by_Tons_River.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
